1. PROJECT NATURE & GOVERNANCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BlitzApp is an independent software project developed to help sports players, 
teams, football stadiums, and game centers discover, schedule, and coordinate 
venue reservations.

* Operating Status:
  This application is operated as a personal, non-commercial developer project 
  without a registered corporate or business entity.

* Intermediary Role:
  BlitzApp serves purely as a technological scheduling tool. BlitzApp does not 
  own, staff, maintain, inspect, or manage any physical stadium or game center 
  facility listed on the platform. All facility conditions, pricing, on-site 
  safety, and match execution remain the direct responsibility of independent 
  venue operators.


2. LEGAL DOCUMENTS INCLUDED IN BLITZAPP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The BlitzApp Legal Hub comprises the following core policy documents:

1. Privacy Policy (privacy-policy.txt):
   - Detailed breakdown of minimal data collection practices (names, usernames, 
     passwords hashed via bcrypt, reservation slots, venue listings).
   - Zero external tracking, zero cross-app data sharing, no behavioral ads.
   - GPS and Google Maps location handling policies (discrete manual manager 
     pins only; no continuous background tracking).
   - User privacy rights and self-service account deletion.

2. Terms and Conditions (terms-and-conditions.txt):
   - User account rules, age eligibility (13+), single-account policy.
   - Customer responsibilities (legitimate bookings, punctuality, fair play).
   - Venue manager responsibilities (accurate listings, price guarantee, 
     honoring confirmed app bookings).
   - Prohibited behaviors (spam bookings, harassment, technical exploits).
   - Limitation of liability regarding physical sports risks and injuries.
   - Governing jurisdiction and dispute resolution framework.

3. Cancellation & Refund Policy (cancellation-and-refund-policy.txt):
   - Step-by-step customer in-app cancellation workflow.
   - Fair play cancellation timelines and anti-no-show guidelines.
   - Venue manager cancellation rules and mandatory reason disclosures.
   - Explanation of on-site cash payment model (no in-app financial transactions 
     or digital escrow refunds).
   - Administrative grievance and dispute resolution process.

4. Account Deletion & Data Erasure Policy:
   - Self-service account deletion accessible directly in-app under 
     Profile > Legal & Compliance > Delete Account.
   - Password verification or typing "DELETE" safeguard.
   - Immediate cancellation and release of upcoming active reservations.
   - Complete erasure or anonymization of profile identifiers, session tokens, 
     and personal data.
   - Anonymized retention of past booking transaction records solely for 
     auditing and venue accounting integrity.


3. ROLES & PARTICIPANTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Customers (Players & Teams):
  Can discover venues, view availability, reserve slots, cancel bookings, 
  manage favorites, and delete their accounts.

* Venue Managers (Stadium & Game Center Operators):
  Can list facilities, set hourly rates in Iraqi Dinars (IQD), manage slot 
  availability, receive booking notifications, review reports, and settle 
  internal 3% platform service fees.

* Platform Administration:
  Maintains system security, audits database logs, monitors no-show reports, 
  and resolves disputes between players and managers.


